                <head>153. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On February 10, 1962, the United States exchanged Colonel Rudolf I. Abel for Francis Gary Powers and Frederick Pryor at the Glienicker
                    Bridge, which linked East and West Berlin. For an account of the exchange by one
                    of the participants, see Donovan, <hi rendition="#italic">Strangers on a
                        Bridge</hi>.</p>
            </div>
